A||||35||88formula||Went to the track today with the 3.4 engine.||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||10-28-2001||05:26 PM|||| I went to the track today for the first time in my life to see how my car would do and to just have fun. It was a blast even though I only got two runs in 4.5 hours time. There where a lot of Mustangs there because they were having the Mustang heads up racing association thing. I saw a Subaru WRX run a 14.1, which looked stock but you never know. I saw a Ford SVT lightening run a 12.9 (WOW for a truck). Many of the Mustangs were running in the low thirteen second range to the high fifteen second range. Some of the Mustangs were in the low nine second range. <P>My first run was horrible. I spun my tires all through first gear and the tachometer rose to 7k+ rpm. Second gear I shifted too high again at 6.2k rpm and the rest I shifted at 6k (hey I was nervous and I can’t drive worth a crap). I made the mistake of driving through the water and not doing a burnout to rid the tires of the water. That is probably one of the reasons why I spun my tires so bad. I tried to launch at 2k rpm, which was too high anyway.<P>My first run looked like this.<BR>R/T   1.256<BR>60’    2.228<BR>330    6.295<BR>1/8     9.683<BR>MPH 73.16<BR>1000 12.589<BR>¼       15.089<BR>MPH  90.21  <P>My second run looked like this.<P>R/T   .720<BR>60’    2.296<BR>330    6.348<BR>1/8     9.7<BR>MPH 73.56<BR>1001 12.627<BR>¼       15.107<BR>MPH  90.84<P>On my second run I avoided the water pit and went straight up to the staging lights. I improved my reaction time but I launched too high again and spun my tires all through first gear and revved it past 7k rpm once again (It happened so fast!). Second gear I shifted at 5500 rpm and the rest I shifted at 5700 rpm. <P>There was basically no traction for the people who didn’t have slicks. First gear for me was basically useless. If I could have hooked up off the line than my 60’ time and ET could have been much better. I basically did a 35’ burnout on every launch.<P>Using this <A HREF="http://www.gordon-glasgow.org/hpcalc.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gordon-glasgow.org/hpcalc.html</A>  web-site I typed in my cars weight with me in it (2975 lbs.), the ET, and the mph to get a rear wheel horsepower and crankshaft horsepower estimate. I got 172.3 rear wheel horsepower and 215.4 crankshaft horsepower. My dyno2000 program estimated the engine to put out 203 horsepower so that’s actually really good. When you consider that NOS3800 ran a 14.86 @ 92.06 MPH with a naturally aspired series two 3800 engine and his engine probably has about the same horsepower than that’s not too far off. Actually if you type in his information and guess that his car weighs about 3000 lbs. than you get 181.7 RWH and 227.1 crankshaft horsepower.<P>Next year I'll do better I hope!      <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||10-28-2001||05:37 PM||||You running a stock 2.8? Need to know cause you're running faster than my best of 15.2 @90mp/h on my stock 4 speed 2.8...<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
