Z||000004||88formula||10-28-2001||05:50 PM||||I can't be that slow because I can slowly pull away from an 88 mustang LX that runs high fourteen second times. I was running with the 3.4 injectors at the time though and now I have the 2.8 injectors. With the 2.8 injectors the top-end isn't as strong as it was with the 3.4 injectors or at least it feels that way. <P>Anyone have any suggestions because these times really do suck! <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Neal||10-28-2001||06:09 PM||||just getting your launch and 60' in order should seat you into the mid 14's.  Looks like your 3.4 is doing a great job!||||reg||1
Z||000006||SKIDMARK||10-28-2001||06:23 PM||||Why did you switch back to the 2.8 injectors? My suggestion is get your launch in order. Gotta get off the line right and the rest of it should fall into place. Don't dump the clutch, slip it just a little. Of course the clutch won't last long but you'll keep the rubber hooked up on the track.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000007||banditbalz||10-28-2001||06:30 PM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierovsmustang_1.jpg">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DrinkMccreery.jpg">   <BR>Looks like I get the thumbs up from a drunk SlammedFiero.... ha ha haaaa<BR>Because of this useless OS (Win 2000 PRO) my scanner isn't working... this is the only slip i had handy. Yeah, I lost to  a Mustang!<BR>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||14
