Z||000009||88formula||10-28-2001||08:08 PM||||I switched back to the 2.8 injectors because the 3.4 injectors where causing too many derivability problems. They where basically no good. My 2.8 injectors where cleaned and flow balanced by Marren Motorsports and they are all I have right now. Next year I'll have the 3.4 injectors blueprinted by Marren and have a custom prom made. To get the engine to not run lean at WOT I had to turn the fuel pressure up to 60 psi and even with the pressure that high the BLM is 140.  <P>Just took the car for a blitz at the light down the street to see what kind of traction I have. I spun through first again without even flooring it and spun halfway through second. The rear end got all squirmy too. I launched as low as I could and then gassed it. I need some better stickier tires!<P>Banditbalz are you bragging? The difference is that you have traction and you’re a better driver than I am. You would have to have about 170 horsepower to get those times or have a really light fiero. <P>Did you say your fiero is stock? Maybe the previous owner did something to it that you don't know about. Are your manifold restrictions ported? <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroKyle||10-28-2001||08:14 PM||||In a few more days later, your gonna need a new set of back tires, lol.||||reg||1
Z||000011||banditbalz||10-28-2001||08:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Banditbalz are you bragging? The difference is that you have traction and you’re a better driver than I am. You would have to have about 170 horsepower to get those times or have a really light fiero. <P>Did you say your fiero is stock? Maybe the previous owner did something to it that you don't know about. Are your manifold restrictions ported? <BR>]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bragging?  Yeah, I guess I am! <BR>I have owned this car for more than 9 years now and have put 176,000 kms on the engine. I have done all the maintenance to the car myself (except clutch and stock ratio tranny). The car is a daily driver and has sit in the leaves, snow, mud, rain and what ever ****  mother nature can throw at her for the last 16 years. Still wins awards in her class. The previous owner (mid 40's) never told me of any mods done to the engine or otherwise. Sure would have been a nice selling feature, don't ya think? I pulled the front manifold off last winter to replace the gasket and I can assure you it isn't ported. Maybe it has a cam in it... Sure doesn't sound like it! Maybe it has higher ratio rockers.... maybe, maybe,....<BR>The engine is stock and in my opinion should be running better than a 15.2!<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||10-28-2001||09:21 PM||||Banditbalz what launch rpm do you use? How do you launch the car? Do you dump the clutch or let it slip a little? What shift points do you use? When you ran the 15.2 did you spin your tires? What were the track and weather conditions? What’s the elevation of the track above sea level? What tire size and kind do you have?<P>I would like to know because for a stock fiero to run a 15.2 is dam impressive. You must be a hell of a good driver to pull that off!<P>O-yeah how much does your fiero weigh? <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||85ZainoGT||10-28-2001||09:39 PM||||wow, a 15.2 stock, that seems crazy, there has to be somthing done to your engine, I can see maybe a 15.7 or 15.8, because I ran a 16.1 and I know it can do more than that, I have an 85gt 4spd.. so.. I dunno<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||banditbalz||10-28-2001||09:42 PM||||I launch at a hair over 3000rpm (eyes are on the xmas tree), probably closer to 3400rpm. I dump the clutch (no slipping) and the tires usually spin (while accelerating) for 10 feet. Rear tire pressure is lowered to 20 psi. I pull as close to redline in 1st gear, second gear i shift before 6000 rpm. Now, this is a bit of a toss-up, but usually I end up shifting 3-4 around 5000rpm. I say a toss-up because I am near redline in 3rd at the end of the Quarter. If I hold it in 3rd, i post slower times (remember this is a Muncie trans.). <BR>Track conditions have always been excellent, except for the fact I have never run on a cold day. That is why I am looking forward to running at Toronto Motorsports Park this sunday.<BR>I am probably lighter than the average driver weighing in at 135lbs. The only lightening I do to the GT is I pull out the 2 bazooka tubes and the spare tire (saves 50-75 lbs).<P>Looking for a 14.9 this sunday.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smack_1.jpg"> <BR>pic of the GT laying the smackdown on a new Miata||||reg||14
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||10-29-2001||12:57 AM||||I raced george from around 30 to 90 mph. I was sticking right with him no probs. (remember the day after your wedding off the corner on the back roads?)<P>I also raced him off a light and got smoked. His car hooks Really really hard.<P><BR>I don't know how to drag race worth a shi* and George has his method of launching the car down perfect.<P>Me thinks in this case..with anyone else driving it , it runs mid 15's. I honestly think it's the driver.<P>Sounds stock to me too. <P>Impressive car.<P>JM ||||reg||1
