Z||000018||GTMike||10-29-2001||03:21 AM||||oh stop.  he didn't flame at all. its true the fiero when tested way back in the 80s were rated at like 0-60 in 8 sec and 1/4 in low 16s or something.  but the fact is that many v6 4 and 5 speed that are very near stock.  have time slips in the mid to low 15s.   <P>i know the 0-60 times sucked because you have to shift in to 3rd gear at like 57 mph. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Slammed Fiero||10-29-2001||08:30 AM||||It can seem strange to whomever , I don't care..<P>I have seen the slips and testimony from several people who witnessed the car run. George is not the kinda person to BS. <P>The dude knows how to launch his car , and drive it hard.<P>Just wait til november 4th , I bet he will run some good #'s.<P>The motor looks to be dead stock. Too quiet for a cam , the heads don't look like they have ever been off ..ect..ect. Trust me I looked!<P>Besdes , George s one person who will tell it like it is.<P>I believe Grinthocks old 85 GT  ran a 15.5 in the 1/4 a few times<P>Magazine drivers are hardly pro's. Few people know how cars are really tested by magazines. I suggest people look for an article called "Up in smoke"  If you read it , you will undestand a lot more about how magazines operate and how #'s are attained.<P>Everyone cries foul when I say I got 6.54 to 60 on several ocasions with a 2.8 and light mods... Yet when I say Fierolisa was in the car when I turned similar times twice , and chris moore saw the GTec flashing after our run (His GTEC)...everyone seems to drop the subject , or ask me if I know how to use it..Ahh aren't you suppose to let it drag on the ground behind the car?<P>Sense the sarcasm?<P>I have to admit , when I first started talkin to george and he told me about his times, I though ..Yeah sure buddy. Then I raced him , and also got a chance to drive the car.. Engine feels real loose , loves to rev.<P>Anyone remember steve huskins? Yellow 85 GT with a fast back conversion. Stock motor except for a MSD , Car is also a 4spd... Recorded several 6.4 sec to sixty and low 15 sec passes.<P>I do believe the Owners of te Fiero Shop in TO were even a bit confused by the whole situation over georges car...<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000020||lou_dias||10-29-2001||12:27 PM||||Using CARTEST.EXE and putting in the numbers for a 3.4 Fiero w/225/60/15 tires I got a dump clutch of 2100 rpm.<P>I've use this effectively at Seekonk Speedway against many cars and have never been beat off the line.<P>My tires chirp then grab and go.||||reg||1
Z||000021||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||12:34 PM||||Magazines testing techniques do vary greatly, no doubt, but those in respectable ones (i.e. motortrend, road and track) are pros.  They have no reason to BS.  If they can really run low 15's im very proud to have ran with one (that makes me what? mid 15's?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
